From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:08:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 075/138] drm: adp: t7000: Time the layer switch by the VBI,
 detect a stalled pipe

On hw, 50 debugfs power off/on cycles while Orchard was page flipping
ended in three underruns and a stalled pipe: frame counter frozen,
IRQ_STATUS RdErr (bit 11), no more VBI, VFTG still running. After that
every DPMS off blocked for ~20 s on flip_done/commit timeouts.

The layer switch was a direct LAYER_CTL write at an arbitrary point of
the frame, and the debugfs path did it unlocked, racing the BASE/STRIDE
writes of in-flight flips.

- LAYER_CTL is now written from the VBI interrupt only: the caller arms
  the value, takes a vblank reference and waits (100 ms max) for the
  handler to write it, then one more frame. Without a usable vblank the
  layer is left on (off path) or written directly as a last resort
  (on path). The CRTC paths now switch the layer while vblank is on:
  before drm_crtc_vblank_off() on disable, after drm_crtc_vblank_on()
  on enable.
- debugfs "power" takes all modeset locks, waits until the CRTC's last
  commit is done with the hardware and has sent its event, and refuses
  (-EBUSY) while the CRTC is off.
- A VBI watchdog runs while vblank is enabled. With no VBI for 300 ms it
  reports the stall with the pipe registers once, masks the block,
  disables the line and switches to the existing 60 Hz hrtimer vblank,
  so flips, vblank waits and DPMS keep completing. iOS treats RdErr,
  PFAlign, PFOver and underrun as fatal and panics; there is no
  in-place recovery to copy, so the screen still needs a reboot.
- debugfs "power" shows the VBI count and the stall state.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
